; --- 37D: the Ashfall Cottage's trophy stands ---------------------------------
; Two authored stands against the room's south wall, so the display slot is reachable the moment the
; cottage is claimed — before the player has crafted anything. More can be placed in the yard with
; the Display Stand kit; both routes build through the same TrophyStandComponent, and a placed one
; reads its holding out of its own place.<propertyId>#<n> id rather than authoring it.
;
; ⚠️ THE PersistentId IS THE SAVE KEY, exactly as for the chest. The one-slot Inventory below IS the
; display, and it persists as inventory:<PersistentId>; without an id it does not register as a
; saveable at all (SaveKeyPolicy.ShouldPersist) and the trophy vanishes on reload, which looks like
; item loss rather than a missing field. Two stands sharing an id is worse — last write wins and one
; trophy silently becomes the other.
;
; Capacity is authored on the node and must stay 1: InventoryComponent.Load restores through
; AddInstance, which clamps to Capacity, so a capacity applied after the save manager's mid-load
; restore would drop the trophy without a word. --validate now enforces the 1 on the placeable
; template for the same reason.

[node name="CottageStandW" type="Node3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -24, 0, -21.5)
script = ExtResource("1_entity")
